1. What is Observer Pattern?
----------------------------
Observer is a Behavioral Design Pattern.

It defines a one-to-many dependency between objects so that when one object
(Subject) changes its state, all dependent objects (Observers) are notified
and updated automatically.

Definition:
"Defines a one-to-many relationship where multiple observers are automatically
notified whenever the subject changes."

---------------------------------------------------------

2. Why do we need Observer Pattern?
-----------------------------------

Problem without Observer:

Suppose we have a Stock class.

class Stock
{
    void priceChanged()
    {
        Email.send();
        SMS.send();
        MobileApp.send();
    }
};

Problems:

❌ Tight coupling
❌ Every new notification requires modifying Stock class
❌ Violates Open/Closed Principle
❌ Difficult to maintain
❌ Difficult to reuse

---------------------------------------------------------

3. Solution
-----------

Create a common Observer interface.

Every notification system implements it.

Subject only knows about Observer interface.

                Observer
                   ▲
      ----------------------------
      |            |             |
   Email       SMS         MobileApp

                 ▲
                 |
              Subject

---------------------------------------------------------

